{
	title: 'Command provenance and nonduplicated outcomes',
	spec: 'Slash-command transcript events preserve the real initiator independently of provider message roles. Commands invoked by Hal through the command tool are durably marked as model-originated, displayed as Hal issued a command in terminal and web, and retain that attribution after reconnect/history loading. Human-issued commands retain human attribution; other-session attribution remains intact. The transcript keeps the tool invocation, command event, and one useful command outcome. Successful rename outcomes say Session renamed: old name → new name, preserving the previous title for reverting. Outputs carry their occurrence timestamp. Terminal command tool results that repeat a visible command outcome do not appear as standalone transcript rows; unmatched results (including validation failures) remain visible. All recorded results stay in history and display state; the terminal tool block link opens the web tool card for full inspection of arguments, results, errors and controls. Web keeps results inside the inspectable tool card, not a separate outcome row. Provider replay is not changed by display suppression. Do not simplify the command tool JSON presentation in this task. Legacy records without explicit provenance remain readable without guessing their origin.',
